  "body": "**What happens:** on upstream/main, four tests in `crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs` fail. Their helper at line 124 builds the expected refusal as \"...re-import with a larger budget (surfaces are approximated to within {mm} mm)\", but since #1074 (the STEP facet budget setting) `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE` reads \"...re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\" (`crates/app/src/model_fidelity.rs:42`). `model_fidelity.rs` and `step_budget.rs` were updated to the new wording; `coarse_laws.rs` was not.\n\n**Evidence:** found by M3's refresh agent running coarse_laws on main 6a10c5ad. `git grep \"re-import with a larger budget\" upstream/main` hits only `coarse_laws.rs:124`.\n\n**Fix:** update the expected text in `coarse_laws.rs:124` to the product wording. Test-only; the refusal itself is unchanged.\n\n**Done means:** `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test coarse_laws` passes on main.\n",
